  "notes": "No people, no violence: the threat and the killing are never drawn; no hands (28 «بسطت إلي يدك»). Light only on «يتقبل الله». The brothers are not named (Al-Muyassar names them, the Quran and As-Sa'di do not). STAGING v4: The two sons of Adam as two faceless men on open land (the place is not given; no names, as only Al-Muyassar names them). The offerings are a symbol only (hands plate on 27:8): no animal, crop or fire, and nothing marks how the acceptance was known (As-Sa'di gives two possibilities). The camera holds on the accepted brother (27:10, the God-fearing one in light robes) then on the other (27:14). The threat is only a speech beat (27:17): no hand, no weapon, no gesture of the killing, no pointing, and no arm gesture at all in the chapter. The other brother answers (27:19, 28:1), shakes his head on 28:6 (he will not stretch his hand) and lowers his head on 28:13 (fearing Allah). Light plate on the acceptance words (27:21). During the warning of the Fire (29:7-13) the camera holds on the wrongdoer and a two-paths plate; nothing literal. The killing (30-31) is in the next video, ambient."
